ll,"attr_info":{"attributes":[{"DocComment":" Acquires a mutex, blocking the current thread until it is able to do so."},{"DocComment":""},{"DocComment":" This function will block the local thread until it is available to acquire"},{"DocComment":" the mutex. Upon returning, the thread is the only thread with the lock"},{"DocComment":" held. An RAII guard is returned to allow scoped unlock of the lock. When"},{"DocComment":" the guard goes out of scope, the mutex will be unlocked."},{"DocComment":""},{"DocComment":" The exact behavior on locking a mutex in the thread which already holds"},{"DocComment":" the lock is left unspecified. However, this function will not return on"},{"DocComment":" the second call (it might panic or deadlock, for example)."},{"DocComment":""},{"DocComment":" # Errors"},{"DocComment":""},{"DocComment":" If another user of this mutex panicked while holding the mutex, then"},{"DocComment":" this call will return an error once the mutex is acquired. The acquired"},{"DocComment":" mutex guard will be contained in the returned error."},{"DocComment":""},{"DocComment":" # Panics"},{"DocComment":""},{"DocComment":" This function might panic when called if the lock is already held by"},{"DocComment":" the current thread."},{"DocComment":""},{"DocComment":" # Examples"},{"DocComment":""},{"DocComment":" ```"},{"DocComment":" use std::sync::{Arc, Mutex};"},{"DocComment":" use std::thread;"},{"DocComment":""},{"DocComment":" let mutex = Arc::new(Mutex::new(0));"},{"DocComment":" let c_mutex = Arc::clone(&mutex);"},{"DocComment":""},{"DocComment":" thread::spawn(move || {"},{"DocComment":"     *c_mutex.lock().unwrap() = 10;"},{"DocComment":" }).join().expect(\"`thread::spawn` should not fail\");"},{"DocComment":" assert_eq!(*mutex.lock().unwrap(), 10);"},{"DocComment":" ```"}],"inline":null,"rename":null,"public":true},"is_local":false,"started_from":false,"is_extern":false,"opacity":"Foreign","lang_item":null,"diagnostic_item":null,"has_errors":false}